1
00:00:08,674 --> 00:00:12,767
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:15,097 --> 00:00:16,400
Air is good.

3
00:00:17,266 --> 00:00:20,032
We have a working relationship.

4
00:00:20,032 --> 00:00:21,504
Okay.

5
00:00:21,504 --> 00:00:27,051
I'm pretty sure nobody followed me
in here, so I've got that going for me.

6
00:00:27,051 --> 00:00:30,259
I have supply concerns about the
air in this room, though.

7
00:00:30,259 --> 00:00:32,243
Business needs to expand.

8
00:00:32,243 --> 00:00:35,767
We need more investors, which I
guess would be plants?

9
00:00:36,676 --> 00:00:38,629
NOT WORMS!

10
00:00:38,629 --> 00:00:41,414
Worms are not conducive to good business.

11
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:44,729
Look at this. They're trying to
take over the market.

12
00:00:44,729 --> 00:00:46,309
I need to withdraw.

13
00:00:46,309 --> 00:00:47,803
I'm taking my assets with me

14
00:00:47,803 --> 00:00:50,434
and I'm going to look for
business opportunities elsewhere.

15
00:00:52,486 --> 00:00:59,551
[underwater panicking]

16
00:00:59,551 --> 00:01:08,084
[underwater mumbling]

17
00:01:08,084 --> 00:01:12,788
[gasping]

18
00:01:12,788 --> 00:01:14,000
This is a tight market.

19
00:01:14,767 --> 00:01:15,434
No matter.

20
00:01:15,815 --> 00:01:20,133
Here at Freeman Industries, we
practice sound investment strategies.

21
00:01:22,761 --> 00:01:26,267
[underwater mumbling]

22
00:01:27,188 --> 00:01:29,907
Okay, don't panic,
don't panic, don't panic.

23
00:01:29,907 --> 00:01:32,830
I'm sure there's minutes' worth
of air in this pocket.

24
00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:33,518
PANIC!

25
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:38,726
[underwater mumbling]

26
00:01:38,726 --> 00:01:41,273
[Right?  No, left!  Left!]

27
00:01:41,273 --> 00:01:47,853
[underwater mumbling]

28
00:01:47,853 --> 00:01:52,832
[gasping, coughing]

29
00:01:52,832 --> 00:01:53,434
Oh.

30
00:01:55,354 --> 00:01:57,045
Jee-yaah, ooh...

31
00:01:57,045 --> 00:01:59,567
Wow, I wouldn't have thought
this was the right way.

32
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:01,400
I'm wet.

33
00:02:02,204 --> 00:02:03,758
Blehblugh!

34
00:02:03,758 --> 00:02:07,007
I wonder if there are places
that do amphibious pizza delivery.

35
00:02:07,007 --> 00:02:09,092
Like by the beach or something.

36
00:02:09,092 --> 00:02:11,127
Damn, I'm kind of hungry, huh?

37
00:02:11,127 --> 00:02:12,501
It's all this swimming.

38
00:02:12,501 --> 00:02:14,716
And beating things to death with a crowbar.

39
00:02:14,716 --> 00:02:16,592
I should've brought some
more snacks with me.

40
00:02:16,592 --> 00:02:19,081
[ichthyosaur roars, scientist screams]

41
00:02:19,081 --> 00:02:21,154
Well, I'm not the only one who's hungry!

42
00:02:21,154 --> 00:02:22,451
Jesus Christ!

43
00:02:22,451 --> 00:02:24,200
Do we keep sharks down here?

44
00:02:24,975 --> 00:02:26,100
Sharks!

45
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:27,000
What the f...

46
00:02:27,744 --> 00:02:30,701
Ah, hold on.  I need to tidy
this place up a bit.

47
00:02:32,630 --> 00:02:33,334
Yuck...

48
00:02:34,677 --> 00:02:38,200
Come to think of it, how much do
I really know about Black Mesa?

49
00:02:41,529 --> 00:02:44,413
We have toxic waste, loads of weapons,

50
00:02:44,413 --> 00:02:47,055
missiles, and now a shark tank.

51
00:02:47,055 --> 00:02:50,501
Am I working for a
James Bond villain company?

52
00:02:50,501 --> 00:02:52,284
I mean, I don't really care, but...

53
00:02:52,284 --> 00:02:53,467
Oh ho!

54
00:02:56,388 --> 00:02:58,434
I don't even know who's
in charge here...

55
00:03:01,382 --> 00:03:05,399
I bet it's some bald guy with a
scar on his face stroking a cat.

56
00:03:05,399 --> 00:03:07,882
Just watching security cameras all day.

57
00:03:07,882 --> 00:03:11,209
We're probably trying to take over
the world and I don't even know it.

58
00:03:11,209 --> 00:03:12,033
What's that say?

59
00:03:12,528 --> 00:03:13,119
Scientist: Did you see--

60
00:03:13,119 --> 00:03:15,870
JESUS CHRIST!  I would've shot you!

61
00:03:15,870 --> 00:03:17,536
SCIENTIST:  --from the Challenger Deep.

62
00:03:17,536 --> 00:03:22,337
SCIENTIST: But I'm positive that beast never
swam in terrestrial waters until a week ago.

63
00:03:22,337 --> 00:03:23,314
It's a shark.

64
00:03:23,314 --> 00:03:26,220
SCIENTIST:  There's a tranquilizer
gun in the shark cage,

65
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:27,257
SCIENTIST: but I'm not sure
What?

66
00:03:27,257 --> 00:03:29,350
SCIENTIST: it would work on this species.

67
00:03:29,350 --> 00:03:30,663
SCIENTIST: You're welcome to try.

68
00:03:30,663 --> 00:03:32,401
Thanks, but I have a real gun.

69
00:03:32,401 --> 00:03:35,896
Tranquilizer... look, I appreciate
wanting to preserve the specimen

70
00:03:35,896 --> 00:03:38,523
in the name of science, but if
that thing gets out of line,

71
00:03:38,523 --> 00:03:40,206
I'm blowing its frigging head off.

72
00:03:40,206 --> 00:03:42,479
Oh, and hey, if
anybody else comes by here,

73
00:03:42,479 --> 00:03:44,566
I need you to be a
character witness for me.

74
00:03:44,566 --> 00:03:45,601
Don't fuck me on this.

75
00:03:46,502 --> 00:03:47,601
Now, what's this say?

76
00:03:48,318 --> 00:03:50,330
I can't read this at all...

77
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:54,525
These look like my old notes when I would
show up to class drunk back in grad school.

78
00:03:54,525 --> 00:03:55,830
That was pretty sweet.

79
00:03:55,830 --> 00:03:57,592
I could get piss drunk most nights

80
00:03:57,592 --> 00:04:00,409
Then hook up an IV to my arm
with a saline solution

81
00:04:00,409 --> 00:04:02,011
and not wake up hung over.

82
00:04:02,011 --> 00:04:03,917
I would just have a buzz instead.

83
00:04:03,917 --> 00:04:06,775
It was awesome having a
med student as a roommate.

84
00:04:06,775 --> 00:04:08,151
Hey, wait, what am I thinking?

85
00:04:08,151 --> 00:04:09,983
That guy said there's animal tranquilizer.

86
00:04:09,983 --> 00:04:11,300
I can get high off of that.

87
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:14,946
I mean, it's pretty crazy stuff, but

88
00:04:14,946 --> 00:04:17,133
these are crazy times!

89
00:04:19,881 --> 00:04:22,920
Yeah, I don't think that shark
could jump this high.

90
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:24,199
Or, can he?

91
00:04:24,199 --> 00:04:26,416
I don't know, better safe than sorry.

92
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,330
Where is he?

93
00:04:29,205 --> 00:04:29,783
Ah!

94
00:04:30,525 --> 00:04:31,190
[ichthyosaur moans]

95
00:04:31,190 --> 00:04:31,945
Yeah!

96
00:04:31,945 --> 00:04:33,793
I killed the shark!

97
00:04:33,793 --> 00:04:35,133
Okay, here we go.

98
00:04:36,455 --> 00:04:37,601
Okay...

99
00:04:38,839 --> 00:04:40,767
Alright, let's take a look.

100
00:04:40,767 --> 00:04:42,869
Dammit, that thing's still alive.

101
00:04:42,869 --> 00:04:44,500
Ah, I don't care.

102
00:04:46,028 --> 00:04:47,801
What's this dart say?

103
00:04:48,208 --> 00:04:50,000
10ccs...

104
00:04:51,137 --> 00:04:51,984
What the hell?

105
00:04:51,984 --> 00:04:53,450
This is Xylazine!

106
00:04:53,450 --> 00:04:55,262
I can't get high off of this!

107
00:04:55,262 --> 00:04:56,274
God dammit!

108
00:04:56,274 --> 00:04:56,934
RARGH!

109
00:04:57,781 --> 00:05:04,319
[underwater panicking]

110
00:05:04,319 --> 00:05:05,343
[ichthyosaur growls]

111
00:05:05,343 --> 00:05:06,464
[crunch]

112
00:05:06,464 --> 00:05:09,567
[barnacle chirping, Gordon choking]

113
00:05:11,148 --> 00:05:12,910
[underwater panicking]

114
00:05:12,910 --> 00:05:14,145
[ichthyosaur growling, crunch]

115
00:05:14,145 --> 00:05:16,677
[gasping]

116
00:05:16,677 --> 00:05:18,322
Go, go, GO, GO!

117
00:05:18,322 --> 00:05:20,267
Aah!  Oh my God!

118
00:05:21,414 --> 00:05:23,775
FUCK YOU, FISH!

119
00:05:23,775 --> 00:05:24,959
Oh, it is on!

120
00:05:24,959 --> 00:05:27,172
You wanna eat me?
I'll give you something to eat.

121
00:05:27,172 --> 00:05:29,891
You think I work at Sea World?
Giving you free food all day?

122
00:05:29,891 --> 00:05:31,569
You're gonna have to pay for this meal.

123
00:05:31,569 --> 00:05:33,323
Come on up, I won't hurt you.

124
00:05:33,323 --> 00:05:34,033
Come on up.

125
00:05:34,412 --> 00:05:35,053
Sucker.

126
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:37,487
[ichthyosaur gurgles]

127
00:05:37,487 --> 00:05:38,651
YEAH!

128
00:05:38,651 --> 00:05:41,067
CALL ME ISHMAEL, BITCH!

129
00:05:41,837 --> 00:05:42,968
Stupid shark...

130
00:05:43,482 --> 00:05:46,075
That takes some of the fight out of you?

131
00:05:46,075 --> 00:05:48,767
Oh!  Almost forgot about you!

132
00:05:49,564 --> 00:05:50,785
Oop, need to reload.

133
00:05:50,785 --> 00:05:58,175
[whistles "Blow the Man Down"]

134
00:05:58,175 --> 00:06:00,332
Looks like I cleaned everything up.

135
00:06:00,332 --> 00:06:02,647
I am a bad ass pool boy.

136
00:06:02,647 --> 00:06:05,287
This water still looks nasty, though.

137
00:06:05,287 --> 00:06:06,834
But I'm not going back.

138
00:06:07,355 --> 00:06:10,968
[underwater humming "Blow the Man Down"]

139
00:06:12,252 --> 00:06:14,534
Okay, more pull ups.

140
00:06:16,941 --> 00:06:19,440
Man, I'm going to be ripped after today.

141
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,534
Now I need to hit the clubs more than ever.

142
00:06:22,212 --> 00:06:24,008
Hell, maybe I still can.

143
00:06:24,008 --> 00:06:27,857
If I get out of state, the feds aren't
going to be looking for me in night clubs.

144
00:06:27,857 --> 00:06:30,601
I'll drive to Dallas.  There's bound to
be something popping there.

145
00:06:30,958 --> 00:06:32,934
Oh, what the hell is this?

146
00:06:33,846 --> 00:06:35,267
Strangle Juncture.

147
00:06:38,130 --> 00:06:41,488
Well, I'm not getting to Dallas
tonight, that's for damned sure.

